%description:

Tcp.fastopenKey:invalid -- a key in another format stops the run with an error at the first cookie.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "in the format of Linux net.ipv4.tcp_fastopen_key
("xxxxxxxx-xxxxxxxx-xxxxxxxx-xxxxxxxx", the primary key)".

The classes: random ("", the default: a key from the RNG), fixed (a key of Linux: the cookie of
8 bytes is that of Linux), invalid (another format: an error at the first cookie), and changed
(the parameter is @mutable: a new key refuses the cookies of the old one). The code:
Tcp::generateFastOpenCookie() reads the key at each cookie that it makes or checks. The cookie
of Linux comes from a Linux run of the packetdrill script fastopen/server/simple1.pkt (inet-gpl):
the key a0bf63f7-ed803d81-cd641d30-cebc4a90 gives the client 10.248.0.2 at the server
192.168.0.2 the cookie 00abaaabe8e954c2 (the script sets these addresses itself).

Host under test: host2, a Fast Open server; host1 requests a cookie at 0.1 s (preconditions).
Observation: the error, and the exit code of the run.

%# parameter: Tcp.fastopenKey
%# class: invalid
%# value: "xyz"
%# key: *.host2.tcp.fastopenKey
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "TcpMutations.h"
#include "TcpTestApp.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpFastopenKeyInvalid")
        .act(action().at(0.1).run<TcpTestApp>("host1.app[0]", [](TcpTestApp& app) { app.socket().connect(app.addressOf("host2"), 1000, true); })
                 .describe("host1 opens connection 1 with Fast Open"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
                  .first()
                  .assertEvent([](const MatchContext& context) {
                      std::string cookie = tcpFastOpenCookieOf(context.event.packet);
                      return cookie == "";
                  })
                  .describe("the SYN of connection 1: a cookie request")
                  .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == true")
             .describe("the SYN-ACK of host2, which the error prevents")
             .within(0.5));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpFastopenKeyInvalid compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host2.tcp.fastopenKey = "xyz"    # the parameter under test
*.host2.tcp.fastopenServerEnabled = true
*.host1.tcp.fastopenClientEnabled = true
*.host1.numApps = 2
*.host1.app[*].typename = "TcpTestApp"
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%exitcode: 1

%contains-regex: stderr
fastopenKey must have the format xxxxxxxx-xxxxxxxx-xxxxxxxx-xxxxxxxx, but it is 'xyz'
